WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.660
Davos Seaworth: What's this one now?

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:05.020
Shireen Baratheon: "The Dance of Dragons,
A True Telling" by Grand Maester Munkun.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.630
Davos: Now that sounds like a proper story.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.630
Stannis Baratheon: What's it about?

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.370
Shireen: It's the story of the fight between
Rhaenyra Targaryen and her half-brother Aegon

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:14.019
for control of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:17.600
Both of them thought they belonged on the
Iron Throne.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:25.449
When people started declaring for one of them
or the other, their fight divided the kingdoms

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:30.619
in two.

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:48.260
Brothers fought brothers, dragons fought dragons.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:01:04.960
By the time it was over, thousands were dead.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:10.729
And it was a disaster for the Targaryens as
well.

00:01:10.729 --> 00:01:11.729
They never truly recovered.

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:13.689
Stannis: The Dance of Dragons.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:15.030
Why is that a dance?

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.909
Shireen: It's just what they call it.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:17.909
Stannis: Hmm.

00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:18.909
Doesn't make much sense.

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:19.909
Shireen: I think it's poetic.

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:23.680
Joffrey Baratheon: Rhaenyra Targaryen was
murdered by her brother, or rather, his dragon.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.750
It ate her while her son watched.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:30.390
Stannis: If you'd had to choose between Rhaenyra
and Aegon, who would you have chosen?

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.700
Shireen: I wouldn't have chosen either.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.460
It's all the choosing sides that made everything
so horrible.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:47.399
Stannis: Sometimes a person has to choose.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:57.282
Viserys Targaryen:The Dance began, as many
dances do, with an old man and a young girl.

00:01:57.282 --> 00:02:01.380
The queen had failed to produce a son for
her king, so he anointed his daughter, the

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.939
Princess Rhaenyra, as his heir.

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:07.840
But years later, the king remarried, and his
new wife, Queen Alicent of House Hightower,

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.670
gave him a son.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.130
Feeble and foolish, the old king refused to
change the succession.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:18.300
He didn't even see how his court had split
into two rival camps of Blacks and Greens,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:25.250
after the dresses that the princess and the
queen had worn to some tourney.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:29.690
One night, a servant found the old king had
died in his sleep and ran to inform Queen

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:31.530
Alicent.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.500
Protocol dictated that the bells would be
rung and a ravensent to Dragonstone to summon

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.830
the heir, Princess Rhaenyra, for her coronation.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:41.670
But Alicent had other plans.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.890
Lord Commander of the Kingsguard, Ser Criston
Cole, summoned the small council to inform

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.370
them of the king's death.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:52.000
Ser Otto Hightower, the Hand of the King and
father to Queen Alicent, demanded that the

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.140
succession be settled immediately.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:59.700
The decrepit old men of the small council
were confused; the succession was settled

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:00.810
in their minds.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:05.420
The old king had forced the lords of Westeros
to swear fealty to Princess Rhaenyra as his

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:06.560
heir.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:12.000
But SerCriston Cole rightly pointed out that
a son comes before a daughter.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:17.390
The council argued until dawn when the Master
of Coin finally stood up and declared he would

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.130
have no part of treason.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:24.770
SerCriston Cole wisely opened his throat with
a dagger, ending the debate.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:28.769
None were more surprised to hear of Prince
Aegon's succession than Prince Aegon himself.

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:33.739
At first, the fool rejected the crown, but
his mother pointed out that his sister Rhaenyra

00:03:33.739 --> 00:03:36.950
would return such loyalty by taking his head.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:42.110
When ravens carried the news of Aegon's coronation
to Dragonstone, Princess Rhaenyra summoned

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.560
her own Black Council.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:48.909
With her was her uncle and husband, Daemon
Targaryen, considered by many to be the most

00:03:48.909 --> 00:03:51.400
dangerous man in Westeros.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.709
Few lords supported her, but the greatest
of these was CorlysVelaryon, who controlled

00:03:55.709 --> 00:04:00.390
the largest fleet in the realm, and his Targaryen
wife Rhaenys, the old king's sister.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:04.230
Then there were her five sons, although none
grown to manhood.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.310
A pitiful assembly, really.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:09.540
Combined they couldn't match the power of
House Hightower alone.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:12.040
But Rhaenyra had dragons.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:19.290
She, Daemon, and Rhaenys rode huge and formidable
beasts, and three of her five sons were riders

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.810
as well.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.910
Dragonstone also housed six more dragons without
riders.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:29.199
Against this, King Aegon had only four dragons
of his own.

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:33.640
Dragons can burn a city, but only armies can
take and hold it.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.729
If she was to prevail, Rhaenyra desperately
needed the support of the few great houses

00:04:37.729 --> 00:04:39.730
not already sworn to Aegon.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:44.620
Her eldest son, Jacaerys, flew to the Vale
and the North, her middle son Lucerys flew

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.100
to the Stormlands.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:51.680
Rhaenyra hoped that the war would begin and,
if the gods were good, end with diplomacy.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.039
As always, they weren't.

00:04:53.039 --> 00:05:00.449
Robert Baratheon:Go home, pup, and tell the
bitch, your mother, that the Lord of Storm's

00:05:00.449 --> 00:05:03.500
End is not a dog she can whistle on.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:08.070
As Aemond's false eyed gleamed at him, the
princeling fled the castle and mounted his

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.920
young dragon Arrax.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:17.090
The rain fell in sheets, and great bolts of
lightning lit the world bright as day.

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:22.730
Arrax was struggling to stay aloft in the
gale when a roar shook the very foundations

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:24.639
of Storm's End.

00:05:24.639 --> 00:05:29.690
Aemond rose through the clouds and below him
the monstrous Vhagar.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:34.231
Prince Lucerys fell, broken, to be swallowed
by the waves.

00:05:34.231 --> 00:05:43.110
With his death, the war of ravens came to
an end, and the war of fire and blood began.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:50.200
Catelyn Stark: When Rhaenyra heard of her
son's death, she collapsed.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:56.500
She considered ending the war right then until
a raven arrived from her husband, Daemon.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.910
Her son would be avenged.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.820
A son for a son.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:06.140
Viserys:Rhaenyra shipped her two youngest
sons across the Narrow Sea for their protection.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:10.750
Only for her youngest to return days later,
clinging to the neck of his wounded and dying

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:11.750
dragon.

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:15.910
He and his brother had been set upon by an
enemy fleet just off Dragonstone.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:20.970
Defying his mother's command, Rhaenyra's eldest
son and heir, Jacaerys, mounted his dragon

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:24.639
Vermaxand flew to rescue his other brother
and punish the enemy fleet.

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:31.100
But the foolish boy let Vermax be hooked like
a trout and dragged into the sea, where he

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.960
soaked up even more arrows than seawater.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:38.509
His brother disappeared over the horizon or
beneath the waves.

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:40.110
No one could say for sure.

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:44.470
With the loss of four dragons, Rhaenyra's
only advantage was fading.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:50.370
Luckily for her, over the centuries, House
Targaryen had spilled more than blood on Dragonstone.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:54.979
She promised gold and title to any of the
Targaryen bastards who could tame the six

00:06:54.979 --> 00:06:57.350
untamed dragons on the island.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:02.449
These bastards were called the dragonseeds,
though most were called supper.

00:07:02.449 --> 00:07:07.500
Perhaps the dragons were eventually sated
or bored, but four of them accepted riders

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.699
and were enlisted in Rhaenyra's cause.

00:07:10.699 --> 00:07:16.290
Robert:King's Landing looked up and saw two
dragons circling their foul city.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:22.200
Daemon and Rhaenyra had come for her throne,
for the city was defenseless.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:29.370
Aemond had taken the king's army from the
city, and worse, he'd taken his dragon Vhagar.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:34.780
Seeing that resistance was hopeless, the small
council surrendered the city, the Queen Mother

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.699
Alicent, and the broken Queen Helaena.

00:07:38.699 --> 00:07:40.419
But not King Aegon.

00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:46.780
Somehow, despite his wounds and delirium,
he had vanished from the city.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:52.720
And so Queen Rhaenyra climbed the steps and
seated herself of the Iron Throne.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:58.639
Legend has it that as she left that hall later,
blood trickled down her legs and hands, proving

00:07:58.639 --> 00:08:01.750
the Iron Throne had spurned her.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:03.200
Nonsense!

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.030
It's a chair made of steel blades.

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:11.340
Rhaenyra had wanted it all her life and had
sacrificed two sons for it.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:15.260
She likely gripped the damn thing too tight.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:20.590
Viserys:Queen Rhaenyra didn't have much time
to grieve for her stupid husband.

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:25.690
The mad former queen Helaena flung herself
from a balcony, to be impaled upon the iron

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.660
spikes lining the moat of Maegor's Holdfast.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:34.440
That night, the city rose in riot against
Rhaenyra, demanding justice for Queen Helaena

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:39.010
and her murdered son, among other foolish
peasantfantasies.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:44.270
In the midst of this chaos, a one-handed fool
called the Shepherd began to rant against

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:45.270
dragons.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.990
Not just the ones of the enemy, but all dragons
everywhere.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:53.959
As he pointed to the Dragonpit above on the
hill, he shouted, "There the demons dwell,

00:08:53.959 --> 00:08:55.320
this is their city.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:58.670
If you would make it yours, first you must
destroy them."

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:04.420
By the time the first of the attackers came
pouring in, all four were roused, awake and

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:05.420
angry.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:07.959
Nobody knows how many men and women died that
night.

00:09:07.959 --> 00:09:08.959
Who cares?

00:09:08.959 --> 00:09:10.470
They all should have!

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:13.760
Trapped within the pit, the dragons could
not fly.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:17.360
Instead, they fought with horns, claws, teeth,
and fire.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:22.950
For every man who died, ten more appeared,
shouting that the dragons must die.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.649
One by one, they did.

00:09:25.649 --> 00:09:30.000
Finally, the last remaining dragon broke her
chain, spread her wings, and flew straight

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.550
up at the great dome trying to flee.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:37.420
Already weakened by dragonflame, the dome
cracked under the force of impact and then

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:41.720
tumbled down, crushing the dragonslayers and
herself.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:47.270
Joffrey Baratheon: High atop the Red Keep,
Queen Rhaenyra clutched her two remaining

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:53.320
sons to her as she watched the end of her
family's might, too afraid of the peasants

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:55.250
to defend her dragons.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:59.340
At least her older son, Joffrey, had a man's
spine.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:04.640
He stole his mother's dragon Syrax and tried
to fly it to the Dragonpit to save his birthright.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:10.900
But the stupid beast didn't understand and
twisted beneath him, fighting to be free of

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:14.780
the little boy, until it was.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:20.650
Weeping for her lost son more than her dragons,
Rhaenyra abandoned the Iron Throne and sold

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:25.899
her crown to buy passage for her and her last
son back to Dragonstone.

00:10:25.899 --> 00:10:29.790
Rhaenyra hoped to hatch more dragons from
the eggs in the castle.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:35.830
But when she landed, the welcoming party slew
her guards and marched her and her son at

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:41.839
spearpoint to the castle to face a dead man
and a dying dragon.

00:10:41.839 --> 00:10:43.019
"Sister!"

00:10:43.019 --> 00:10:46.300
King Aegon, Second of His Name, called out
to Rhaenyra.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:53.540
Rook's Rest had left Aegon bent and twisted,
his once handsome face puffy from milk of

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:57.920
the poppy, with burn scars covering half his
body.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:03.180
Rhaenyra, ever defiant, told her dear brother
that she'd hoped he was dead.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.139
"After you!"

00:11:05.139 --> 00:11:06.910
Aegon answered.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:17.690
Then Sunfyre bathed her in a blast of flame
and devoured her in six bites while her son

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:53.639
watched, leaving the seventh and final bite,
her lower leg, for the Stranger.

